## In 30 seconds

Declare a service extending **AbstractCRUDRestService** with `@RestTarget` / `@RestPath`. JAX-RS `Client` comes from **ClientProviderService**. Call `doGetObjects`, `doCreateObject`, etc. on a background thread, or listen for generated wave types in `initWave()`.

Quick Start
---------------------

Add the REST module and declare a typed service. REST calls run on background threads via the standard JRebirth Service lifecycle.

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.jrebirth.af</groupId>
    <artifactId>rest</artifactId>
    <version>${jrebirth.version}</version>
</dependency>
```

**Minimal example — CRUD service for a `Planet` resource:**

```java
@RestTarget(value = "http://localhost:8080/JRebirth")
@RestPath("planets")
public class PlanetRestService extends AbstractCRUDRestService<Planet> {

    @Override
    public Class<Planet> objectClass() {
        return Planet.class;
    }
}
```

**Trigger a GET from any component:**

```java
PlanetRestService service = getService(PlanetRestService.class);
List<Planet> planets = service.doGetObjects(null);
```

Configure server defaults in `jrebirth.properties` when you omit parts of `@RestTarget` (see RestParameters below).


REST
==============


Overview
---------------------

The JRebirth REST module (`org.jrebirth.af:rest`) provides a service-based approach to communicating with REST APIs from JavaFX applications. It integrates with JAX-RS clients and follows the standard JRebirth Service lifecycle, allowing REST calls to be triggered via Waves and executed on background threads without blocking the JavaFX Application Thread.

Key features:

* Annotation-driven server and path configuration
* Pluggable JAX-RS Client provider
* Abstract base classes for generic and CRUD-specific REST services
* Configuration via JRebirth ParameterItems


AbstractRestService
---------------------

**AbstractRestService** is the base class for all REST services. It extends `AbstractService` and handles HTTP client lifecycle management. During initialization, it:

1. Reads the `@RestTarget` annotation to build the base URL.
2. Reads the `@RestPath` annotation to determine the local path segment.
3. Obtains a JAX-RS `Client` instance from the linked `ClientProviderService`.

Subclasses must implement `initWave()` to register the WaveTypes they handle.


```java
@Override
protected void initService() {
    final RestTarget rt = ClassUtility.getLastClassAnnotation(this.getClass(), RestTarget.class);
    final StringBuilder url = new StringBuilder();
    if (rt != null && rt.value() != null) {
        url.append(rt.value());
    } else {
        url.append(rt.protocol().name())
           .append("://").append(rt.address())
           .append(":").append(rt.port())
           .append("/").append(rt.path());
    }
    baseWebTarget = clientProvider.client().target(url.toString());

    final RestPath rp = ClassUtility.getLastClassAnnotation(this.getClass(), RestPath.class);
    if (rp != null) {
        localPath = rp.value();
    }
    initWave();
}

protected WebTarget webTarget() {
    return baseWebTarget().path(localPath());
}
```

`initService()` resolves the base URL from `@RestTarget` (full `value()` or decomposed parts with `RestParameters` fallbacks), then applies `@RestPath` through `webTarget()`.

AbstractCRUDRestService
---------------------

**AbstractCRUDRestService** extends `AbstractRestService` and provides a complete set of CRUD operations on a typed resource. It implements the `CRUDRestService<O>` interface with the following operations:

* `doCreateObject(O object, Wave wave)` &mdash; sends a POST request to create a resource.
* `doUpdateObject(O object, Wave wave)` &mdash; sends a PUT request to update a resource.
* `doDeleteObject(Object object, Wave wave)` &mdash; sends a DELETE request to remove a resource.
* `doGetObject(Integer id, Wave wave)` &mdash; sends a GET request to retrieve a single resource.
* `doGetObjects(Wave wave)` &mdash; sends a GET request to retrieve all resources.


```java
@Override
public List<O> doGetObjects(final Wave wave) {
    return baseWebTarget()
        .request(MediaType.APPLICATION_XML)
        .get(genericList);
}

@Override
public boolean doCreateObject(O object, final Wave wave) {
    final Response response = baseWebTarget()
        .request(MediaType.APPLICATION_XML)
        .post(Entity.xml(object));
    return response.getStatusInfo() == Status.OK;
}
```

Override `objectClass()` and optionally `localPath()` / `initWave()` to register wave listeners. HTTP verbs map to JAX-RS calls on `baseWebTarget()` or `webTarget()`.


CRUDRestService Interface
---------------------

The **CRUDRestService** interface defines the contract for CRUD operations and declares wave item constants used for wave communication:


```java
public interface CRUDRestService<O extends Object> extends Service {

    /** The Wave Item Element. */
    WaveItem<Object> ELEMENT = new WaveItemBase<Object>() {
    };

    String CREATE_OBJECT_PREFIX = "CREATE_OBJECT_";

    String OBJECT_CREATED_PREFIX = "OBJECT_CREATED_";

    // WaveType DO_CREATE_OBJECT = WBuilder.waveType(CREATE_OBJECT)
    // .returnAction(OBJECT_CREATED)
    // .items(ELEMENT)
    // .returnItem(JRebirthItems.booleanItem);

    String UPDATE_OBJECT_PREFIX = "UPDATE_OBJECT_";

    String OBJECT_UPDATED_PREFIX = "OBJECT_UPDATED_";

    // WaveType DO_UPDATE_OBJECT = WBuilder.waveType(UPDATE_OBJECT)
    // .returnAction(OBJECT_UPDATED)
    // .items(ELEMENT)
    // .returnItem(JRebirthItems.booleanItem);

    // @OnWave(CREATE_OBJECT)
    // @Priority(PriorityLevel.Normal)
    boolean doCreateObject(O object, final Wave wave);

    // @OnWave(UPDATE_OBJECT)
    // @Priority(PriorityLevel.Normal)
    boolean doUpdateObject(O object, final Wave wave);

    // @OnWave(CREATE_OBJECT)
    // @Priority(PriorityLevel.Normal)
    boolean doDeleteObject(O object, final Wave wave);

    // @OnWave(CREATE_OBJECT)
    // @Priority(PriorityLevel.Normal)
    O doGetObject(Integer id, final Wave wave);

    // @OnWave(CREATE_OBJECT)
    // @Priority(PriorityLevel.Normal)
    List<O> doGetObjects(final Wave wave);

}
```


@RestTarget
---------------------

The **@RestTarget** annotation defines the target server URL for a REST service. It supports two modes:

* **Full URL** &mdash; set `value()` to the complete base URL string.
* **Decomposed** &mdash; specify individual parts: `protocol()`, `address()`, `port()`, and `path()`.

When individual parts are not specified, they fall back to `RestParameters` defaults.


```java
@Target(ElementType.TYPE)
@Retention(RetentionPolicy.RUNTIME)
@Inherited
@Documented
public @interface RestTarget {

    enum Protocol {
        http, https
    }

    String value();

    Protocol protocol() default Protocol.http;

    String address() default "";

    int port() default 80;

    String path() default "";

}
```


@RestPath
---------------------

The **@RestPath** annotation defines the local endpoint path appended to the base URL for a specific REST service.


```java
@Target(ElementType.TYPE)
@Retention(RetentionPolicy.RUNTIME)
@Inherited
@Documented
public @interface RestPath {

    String value();

}
```


ClientProviderService
---------------------

The **ClientProviderService** interface defines the contract for providing JAX-RS `Client` instances. The default implementation, **SimpleClientProviderService**, creates a standard JAX-RS client on initialization and closes it when the service is released.

It is registered with `@Register(ClientProviderService.class)` so it can be replaced by a custom implementation if needed.


```java
@Register(ClientProviderService.class)
public class SimpleClientProviderService extends AbstractService implements ClientProviderService {

    private Client client;

    @Override
    public Client client() {
        return client;
    }

    @Override
    protected void initService() {
        client = ClientBuilder.newClient();
    }

    /**
     * When the service is released close the client.
     */
    @OnRelease
    public void closeClient() {
        client.close();
    }

    @Override
    protected void processWave(Wave wave) {
        // Nothing to do yet
    }

    @Override
    protected void initInnerComponents() {
        // Nothing to do yet
    }

}
```


RestParameters
---------------------

**RestParameters** provides configurable default values for REST server connection properties. These are used as fallbacks when `@RestTarget` attributes are not explicitly set:

| Parameter | Default | Description |
|-----------|---------|-------------|
| `DEFAULT_REST_SERVER_PROTOCOL` | `http` | Protocol (http/https) |
| `DEFAULT_REST_SERVER_ADDRESS` | `localhost` | Server hostname |
| `DEFAULT_REST_SERVER_PORT` | `8080` | Server port |
| `DEFAULT_REST_SERVER_PATH` | `JRebirth` | Base context path |

These can be overridden in your application's `jrebirth.properties` file.


Usage Example
---------------------

### Step 1 — Define the resource type ###

```java
public class Planet {
    private String name;
    // getters / setters
}
```

### Step 2 — Declare the REST service ###

```java
@RestTarget(protocol = Protocol.http, address = "localhost", port = 8080, path = "JRebirth")
@RestPath("planets")
public class PlanetRestService extends AbstractCRUDRestService<Planet> {

    @Override
    public Class<Planet> objectClass() {
        return Planet.class;
    }
}
```

### Step 3 — Call from a Model or Service ###

```java
@Override
protected void initModel() {
    PlanetRestService planets = getService(PlanetRestService.class);
    List<Planet> all = planets.doGetObjects(null);
}
```

Wave-driven usage is also supported: override `initWave()` in your subclass to `listen()` for the generated `DO_CREATE_OBJECT`, `DO_GET_OBJECTS`, etc. wave types.


